# Cell from playpick: mode=daily, boss=saved (coverage label only -- a daily's
# boss is drawn from the UTC date, not choosable; direction.md's driver-lesson
# note says record it after the fact, don't aim for it), spec=warrior:
# protection, style=good, view=844x390,touch, save=carried (behaves as fresh
# per #273).
#
# Probe (2026-09-26-45-probe.play) found today's actual daily is The Three
# Crowns, 25-player normal, SWARMING -- the same instance a same-day session
# already fought three times: hunter:marksmanship/melee twice
# (2026-09-26-21/-22-finish, both landed the whole fight on the untouchable
# decoy body, aliveParty=25/25, boss 10-20% by 218-257s) and paladin:holy/idle
# once (2026-09-26-39, tracked the melee pulls closely, aliveParty=25/25,
# boss 15% by 258s). Both prior styles never once solved the crown puzzle
# because src/main.ts:2910's hud() exposes only one boss actor's position,
# nothing about which of the three court bodies currently holds the crown --
# direction.md flagged this as a real driver-vocabulary gap, not yet tested
# under `good` or on a tank spec.
#
# This session is both: the first `good`-style pull of The Three Crowns (good
# does compute an away-from-standing-ground term, unlike melee's pure beeline,
# so this checks whether that term does anything for a fight whose danger is
# who-is-marked rather than where-the-ground-hurts) and the first tank spec on
# this fight (a protection warrior has taunt/threat tools a real player would
# use to pull the crown deliberately, that `good`'s scripted style does not
# call). Expect the same blind spot direction.md already predicts -- worth
# confirming on a fourth style/first tank rather than guessing it generalises.
#
# Reached via the daily screen directly (no invite hash needed -- the daily is
# open to any class/spec on any save state, per README's "the day picks the
# fight, you pick the class"). Unlike the raid setup screen, the daily's class
# grid exposes only indexed tiles (class:0..class:16), not named ones -- the
# probe's targets/screenshot confirmed class:0 is "Warrior Tank" -- and its
# button is named "start", not "pull" (both learned the hard way: the first
# attempt at this script used the named/pull forms from the raid-setup
# vocabulary and got two no-such-control faults plus a screen-never-came,
# never actually starting a fight).
open
tap daily
tap class:0
tap start
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot open

play good 90
bill
state
shot mid1

play good 90
bill
state
shot mid2

play good 90
bill
state
says
shot end

play good 30
bill
state
says
shot finish
